ere for a year before they can move on  to the Spanish mainland hardly any of  them apply for asylum their chances of  getting it are next to none the town of  just 80,000 is struggling to cope with  the added burden a city councilor  accuses Spain of leaving them to deal  with the problem on their own they have  to respect the borders we can't have the  migrants attacking our fence the  theabout up or there and we don't have  the capacity to take in everyone that  would be impossible  data is impossible a thorough checks at  suitors border crossing are the norm so  are the hours of waiting twenty thousand  people enter and exit every day many  Moroccans live from the trade with this  autonomous Spanish town  watching the border is a Herculean task  for Alfonso Cruzado and the gardius  Seville about 600 staff are always on  duty they use video cameras to monitor  the fences various sections as well as  the sea in the Strait of Gibraltar the  team has reached their limits Casa de  personas is taken together it's no  simple thing to hold off huge crowds of  people  the Moroccan authorities and ours need a  very good working relationship if both  sides coordinate their efforts and  things go smoothly we achieve our  objectives  Sheikh Omar Knievel the young man in the  hills of Morocco have also realized  their strength in numbers Salif and his  friends are planning their next attempt  now they also want to escape the  brutality of the Moroccan police they  get their food from a nearby garbage  dump a soft drink a cucumber a moldy  potato life here is unbearable Morocco  is teeming with cops all my friends who  left Kimi with me have made it as far as  they why should I stay Morocco I'll stay  until I eventually get in God willing it  can be hard to distinguish courage from  desperation for Salif and his friends  it's Europe or bust
 

